staging a complex stunt or a giant set  piece is a massive challenge these  achievements are incredible to watch but  learning about what needed to happen  behind the scenes only makes us  appreciate them more here's a look at  some iconic movie scenes that were  nearly impossible to capture on film  Fast Five as quick-moving as its title  suggests Fast Five is at its best  during the climactic car chase through  the streets of Rio protagonist DOM and  Brian have to drag a 100 ton bank vault  behind them with the police hot on their  tail  it's such an enormous set piece that it  would be totally understandable to  assume it's mostly CGI instead it's  nearly all practical effects director  Justin Lin was adamant about using as  little CGI as possible so stunt  coordinator Jack Gill built a replica  vault that weighed 10,000 pounds  although lighter than a real metal vault  it still required souped-up cars with  oversized tires and 400 horsepower  engines so that they could actually  swing around the replicas when you're  watching DOM and Brian swing a vault  through buildings and cement like a  wrecking ball that's actually happening  somewhat surprisingly no one was hurt in  the scenes filming Mission Impossible  Ghost Protocol the mission impossible  franchise has mostly become a series of  films where we watched Tom Cruise Jeep  death over and over  actually scary coolness but all other  stumps pale in comparison next to the  tower climbing sequence and Mission  Impossible Ghost Protocol this sequence  Seas Cruises Ethan Hunt climbing the  exterior of the Burj Khalifa the tallest  building in the world  crews actually fired the film's  insurance company so he could perform  the climb without a stunt double with  only some rigging between him and the  ground what's more there was no way to  cushion Cruz's landing during the  climactic jump back onto the tower he  just went for it landing full force on  the glass Iron Man 3  sometimes a well performed practical  effects stunt actually looks like CGI  because of how impossible it seems case  in point the breathtaking airplane  rescue set piece from Iron Man 3  remember that game called barrel of  monkeys that's a rarity of 18,000  people everybody grab me monkey in order  to shoot the scene without CGI the  filmmakers began with two days of  testing at the airport to make sure it  could even work once they determined it  was possible they proceeded to make the  jump multiple times a day all alongside  a cameraman days to shoot it we ended up  making 62 airplane loads over 600  parachute jumps 480 some hidden  parachute jumps the extra effort of  using practical effects resulted in a  genuinely thrilling action sequence  cliffhanger 1993's cliffhanger is a  perfect example of a dangerous stunt  making a movie a classic one  jaw-dropping scene involves a character  traveling from one airplane to another  via a single cable the planes had to  travel at an exact speed of 150 miles  per hour each if either sped up stuntman  Simon Crain could have been ripped in  half  any faster and the force of the wind  would likely pull cranes limbs from his  torso the altitude and wind created  numbing temperatures as well with crane  having to dawn a special prosthetic  facemask in order to endure the cold  luckily cream managed to perform the  stunt almost perfectly except for some  trouble getting pulled into the second  plane the door  bounce bounce again and that's when I  hit went above and slid along the roof  cranes death-defying stunt is as  breathtaking now as it was when the film  first came out Ben Hur shooting a  biblical drama in the 1950s offered very  little room for cinematic sleight of  hand and 1959's Ben Hur was no different  the famous chariot race took nearly a  year to prepare with the million dollar  arena set carved out of a quarry by a  thousand workmen among other intense  preparations I went over  the shoot itself required nearly a  hundred trained racehorses that actually  ended up being faster than the car  carrying the camera  this gave the cameramen only a few  seconds to get each shot per take even  with a head start in addition the heat  limited the horses to eight runs a day  and a stunt gone wrong  very nearly resulted in stuntman joka  nut being trampled by his horses and  chariots  despite everything the filmmakers and  crew managed to pull the whole thing off  for that alone they deserved all 11 of  the Oscars the film received Raiders of  the Lost Ark Indiana Jones and the  Raiders of the Lost Ark is chock-full of  some of the most memorable imagery in  film history one particularly famous  stunt proved more difficult than others  the sequence in which Harrison Ford's  stuntman Terry Leonard is dragged along  a dirt road behind a speeding truck  despite the fact that Leonard only  drifts under the truck for six seconds  the stunt was immensely dangerous thank  belief Leonard came away unscathed  pulling off one of the greatest stunts  of all time  [Music]
 

